      "finding_id": "F-2",
      "decision": "pushed_back",
      "source_file": "src/sqllens/memory/store.py",
      "claim_text": "One worker with an unbounded queue: a hung ChromaDB call stalls every later memory tool call forever with no timeout, no caller error and no log line",
      "skip_category": "uncategorized",
      "evidence": "Design decision the issue settled: issue #303 Implementation Notes choose one process-wide ThreadPoolExecutor(max_workers=1) and reject other executors; a wait timeout would let a write still queued or running be reported as failed while it later takes effect, a semantic the issue and criteria leave open. The trade-off is disclosed in docs/internal/mcp-server/transport.md (Trade-offs: 'A store call that hangs now stalls later memory tool calls instead of the whole server'). Revisit if a hung ChromaDB call is observed or a bounded-wait design is decided."
    },
    {
      "finding_id": "F-3",
      "decision": "pushed_back",
      "source_file": "src/sqllens/memory/store.py",
      "claim_text": "A nested run_memory_call from code already on the memory worker deadlocks silently; only the docstring guards it",
      "skip_category": "claim-quality",
      "evidence": "No caller sends the nested input: run_memory_call's callers are server.py memory handlers (542, 566, 591, 620, 695, 729) and importer.py 76, all event-loop coroutines; the functions they pass (memory.admin functions, importer._baseline) never call run_memory_call.",
      "parking_evidence": {
        "basis": "a runtime guard would cover an input no caller sends",
        "failing_input": "run_memory_call invoked from a function already running on the sqllens-memory worker",
        "source": "src/sqllens/memory/importer.py:76 and src/sqllens/server.py:542-729 call sites",
        "finding_ref": {
          "iter": 1,
          "index": 3
        }
      }
    },
    {
