      "description": "run_memory_call (src/sqllens/memory/store.py 88-99) attaches nothing to the concurrent future; when the awaiting task is cancelled after the store call starts, asyncio drops the worker's result or exception and nothing logs it. A failing delete_memory / clear_memories / import_memory baseline (clear=True) call whose caller was cancelled loses its error (handler logger.exception at server.py 599-603, 623-627 already unwound with CancelledError), and a successful delete or wipe leaves no log line. Regression versus the on-loop design; the SQL pool's precedent is sql_threads.py 119-122, 157 (future.add_done_callback(_log_call_after_cancel)). Tests cover only ordering of a cancelled delete, not its outcome.",
